# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# What the assembly of the loop over frames assumes of the text that the
# builder emits (#302, #309) on a GPU, in double and mixed precision: the
# text of the loop, the stack of the entry at the boundary, to the byte, and
# the bytes in use of the allocator of the host from frame 101 to frame 201
# (#306: what the host and the runtime of the device keep for a frame), as
# python-frames-loop.test has them. On a GPU the rows of the evaluation,
# which stand in the loop, are taken at every frame and given back where the
# iteration ends: the lowering releases the stack of each iteration of a
# loop of the host.
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frames.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide loop GPU Double | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frames.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide loop GPU Mixed | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Mixed"
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the loop over frames of the whole potential: {{.*}}; in it 0 calls in the generic form, 0 arguments of the entry that a frame replaces, 0 allocations of the stack of a size that is not a constant; {{[1-9][0-9]*}} allocations of the stack of a constant size in it: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the loop over frames of the dependent terms: {{.*}}; in it 0 calls in the generic form, 0 arguments of the entry that a frame replaces, 0 allocations of the stack of a size that is not a constant; {{[1-9][0-9]*}} allocations of the stack of a constant size in it: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the loop over frames of a program with a barostat: {{.*}}; in it 0 calls in the generic form, 0 arguments of the entry that a frame replaces, 0 allocations of the stack of a size that is not a constant; {{[1-9][0-9]*}} allocations of the stack of a constant size in it: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the loop over frames of a triclinic cell: {{.*}}; in it 0 calls in the generic form, 0 arguments of the entry that a frame replaces, 0 allocations of the stack of a size that is not a constant; {{[1-9][0-9]*}} allocations of the stack of a constant size in it: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the stack of the entry of the whole potential at the boundary after frames 1, 101, and 201: {{[0-9]+}} bytes, then +0 and +0 bytes (bound 0): True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the bytes in use of the allocator with the whole potential from frame 101 to frame 201: {{.*}} (bound 64): True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the stack of the entry of the dependent terms at the boundary after frames 1, 101, and 201: {{[0-9]+}} bytes, then +0 and +0 bytes (bound 0): True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the bytes in use of the allocator with the dependent terms from frame 101 to frame 201: {{.*}} (bound 64): True
# CHECK: loop passed
